19. Maya Gopinathan Vs. Anoop S.B.and Another, the Hon'ble Supreme Court held at para 20 is as follows ;
20. Law is well-settled that inference from the evidence and circumstances must be carefully distinguished from conjectures or speculation.

In civil cases including matrimonial 2024 see Online SC 609 //11// disputes of a civil nature, the standard of proof is not proof beyond reasonable doubt 'but' the preponderance of probabilities tending to draw an inference that the fact must be more probable.
